From: Studio (C1), 2026-11-10 — the approval lane (STUDIO-11; main's go; dc-r8-selection-before-generation layer 3)
Subject: a scripted remediation marked `piece` asks Studio for the approved piece of its mix-up

The approval lane stores generated pieces approved offline (data/studio-approved: predicate checks, a render at p360 / p412 /
l1366, a separate Claude judge), each FOR one mix-up of one topic. A remediation already fires only for the child who showed
that mix-up (scriptBeat.beatId "rem:<misconceptionId>"), so the beat is the selection: when Learning's script marks the
remediation entry `"piece": true` (to-learning/006), this carries `piece: true` onto its scriptBeat (both remediation paths in
state.js) and onto the whiteboard ask (propose.js refOf). Studio's seam (requestIntent) then reveals the approved piece for that
mix-up when the tray gate passes it at the child's device size, and the script's own board otherwise — so nothing changes for
a remediation not marked, or a mix-up with no approved piece. Her line points at the piece from its facts row (the slot's
facts, as for any Studio piece); the piece holds the tray while the child plays it (it is not a board).

Two lines. Apply with `git apply` on the Brain branch.

